# ANCHORED to the repository root during the 2026-08-28 template migration.
# This line used to read "index.md", unanchored, which git applies at EVERY depth.
# Before the migration the repository had no input/pagecontent/, so it never mattered;
# afterwards it silently swallowed the guide's home page in BOTH languages, and the
# IG Publisher failed in CI with "Template based HTML file index.html is missing
# source file index.md" while building green locally, where the untracked file exists.
/index.md
/input-cache
/output
/temp
/template

.history

validation.html
/fsh-generated/resources/ImplementationGuide-mii-ig-molgen*

# FHIR Validator
validator_cli.jar

# MCP configuration (contains local paths)
.mcp.json

# Simplifier Bake output
.bake/
.simplifier/
package.bake.yaml
project.yaml

# Ballot documentation
Ballotierung*.pdf

# Package artifacts
*.tgz

# ---- appended from mii-kds-module-template v0.13.0 (IG-template migration) ----
output/
temp/
template/
input-cache/
# NOT ignored wholesale, deliberately. The MII-wide shared workflow
# medizininformatik-initiative/kerndatensatz-meta/.github/workflows/ci_dotnet_validation.yml
# -- which BOTH .github/workflows/validation.yml (the module template's) and the
# repository's own main.yml call -- runs SUSHI and then COMMITS fsh-generated/resources/
# back to the branch. Ignoring the directory makes that step fail with
# "The following paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files: fsh-generated".
# The module template gitignores it because it treats generated output as a build
# artefact; the template's own CI never hits the conflict, because validation.yml
# skips these jobs on the template repository itself. The already-migrated sibling
# module kerndatensatz-biobank commits fsh-generated/ and ignores only the three
# churn files below -- that is the configuration a real MII module needs, so it is
# the one used here. See DEC-4 in migration-log/migration-report.md.
/fsh-generated/data/fsh-index.json
/fsh-generated/fsh-index.txt
/fsh-generated/includes*
publisher.jar
node_modules/
*.log
# ...but NOT the migration audit trail. migration-log/ IS the evidence the
# migration report cites: the run log, and the raw output of every step behind
# every number in it. The bare *.log above (from the module template) would
# have dropped all of it from git, which is the same unanchored-pattern class
# as the /index.md line above.
!migration-log/**
